invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the ALPN arm matches an offered protocol by length alone, so a
  server that names "h3" is answered with the index of the two-byte
  protocol the client did offer. RFC 7301 §3.2 gives the server no way
  to select outside the offer, and the caller would then speak a
  protocol the server never chose. bin/handshake_strict_webpki's
  unoffered and prefix rows object.

